# Copy to .env.development (or .env.production for prod builds) and edit as needed.
# .env* files are gitignored — never commit real URLs.

# API base URL — the frontend calls this origin + /api/v1/birth-death/mlc,
# /api/v1/birth-death/mlr, /api/v1/deaths, etc.
#
# Points straight at certificate-serv, NOT the API Gateway. Two reasons:
#   1. This module has no login page and no host (web-ui) bridge when run
#      standalone, so it has no way to obtain a real JWT — and the gateway
#      enforces its own auth check independently of the backend's profile.
#   2. certificate-serv's SecurityConfig (TOKENLESS_PROFILES: docker/dev/local)
#      bypasses JWT validation entirely when the deployed instance is running
#      one of those profiles — which the dev deployment at
#      certificate.pomodoro.help is, so direct calls succeed without a token.
# If this module is later embedded in web-ui (which supplies a real token via
# window.__swasthea_ensure_token) or the backend moves to a non-tokenless
# profile, switch this to the gateway origin instead — see
# birth-death-registration-ui/.env.example for that pattern.
#
# Leave unset in dev to use the Vite proxy (see vite.config.ts) against a
# locally-running backend instead.
# Default: https://certificate.pomodoro.help
VITE_MLC_MLR_API_BASE_URL=https://certificate.pomodoro.help
